  "name": "DESMOGLEIN - 3 ANTIBODY VESICOBULLOUS DISORDERS",
  "code": "2722",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong>Medical Remarks:</strong>&nbsp;Correlation with clinical history is suggested.</span></p>\n<h3><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong><u>Interpretation:</u></strong></span></h3>\n<ol>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">In mucosal predominant Pemphigus vulgaris (PV) - desmoglein-3 (Dsg3) autoantibodies are present .</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">In mucocutaneous PV - antibodies to both Dsg1 and Dsg3 are present .</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">In Pemphigus foliaceus (PF) antibodies to Dsg1 are present and not to Dsg3</span></li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">The severity of skin and oral disease in pemphigus is determined by the quantities of desmoglein-1 (Dsg1) and desmoglein- 3 (Dsg3) antibodies .</span></li>\n</ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"><strong><u>Associated Test:</u></strong></span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Epidermal antibodies by IF (immunofluoroscence method)</span></p>",
